Speed and memory options for OneJev's trainer (train/sft.py, train/common.py), used to train SpecOne-4B.
Modifications by the SpecOne authors to OneJev (https://github.com/OmniJev/OneJev, Apache-2.0) at commit
0b9e163f8114f94a40598c59b0bac473ff446f3c. None of them changes the loss, the data order or the gradient:
  --fwd-split K          run each micro-batch as K forward/backward chunks (activation memory only)
  --attn-impl NAME       attn_implementation passed to from_pretrained (e.g. flash_attention_2)
  --prefetch-workers N   render rows and run the processor in N DataLoader workers, forked once for all epochs
  --prefetch-timeout S   fall back to inline preparation if a worker stalls
  --tf32                 allow TF32 for fp32 matmuls and convolutions
  --save-epochs          also save the weights at the end of every epoch but the last
Apply inside the OneJev checkout:  git apply /path/to/SpecOne/patches/onejev-speed.patch

